            <ArticleTitle>Double balloon angioplasty for unstentable large-caliber right coronary stenosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E52-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite newer lower-profile stent technologies, placing coronary stents may still remain challenging when vessels are extremely tortuous. We describe a case of a tortuous, very largecaliber right coronary with a near-180 degrees switchback &quot;shepherd's crook&quot; turn, which could not be stented, and for which double balloon angioplasty was successfully performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
